{"surah": 46, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "حمٓ ", "translation": "Ḥā, Meem.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "حمٓ", "translit": "ٓmḥ", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "تَنزِيلُ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْحَكِيمِ ", "translation": "The revelation of the Book is from Allāh, the Exalted in Might, the Wise.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تَنزِيلُ", "translit": "ُlyِznَt", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْكِتَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰtِkْlٱ", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزِ", "translit": "ِzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْحَكِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِkَḥْlٱ", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "مَا خَلَقْنَا ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَآ إِلَّا بِٱلْحَقِّ وَأَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّىۚ وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ عَمَّآ أُنذِرُوا۟ مُعْرِضُونَ ", "translation": "We did not create the heavens and earth and what is between them except in truth and [for] a specified term. But those who disbelieve, from that of which they are warned, are turning away.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "خَلَقْنَا", "translit": "āَnْqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضَ", "translit": "َḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَيْنَهُمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmُhَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱِb", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَأَجَلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَjgَaʾَw", "root": "اجل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مُّسَمًّى", "translit": "àًّmَsُّm", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَمَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّmَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أُنذِرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrِhdnُaʾ", "root": "نذر"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مُعْرِضُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḍِrْʿعُm", "root": "عرض"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "قُلْ أَرَءَيْتُم مَّا تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ أَرُونِى مَاذَا خَلَقُوا۟ مِنَ ٱلْأَرْضِ أَمْ لَهُمْ شِرْكٌ فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِۖ ٱئْتُونِى بِكِتَٰبٍ مِّن قَبْلِ هَٰذَآ أَوْ أَثَٰرَةٍ مِّنْ عِلْمٍ إِن كُنتُمْ صَٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "Say, [O Muḥammad], \"Have you considered that which you invoke besides Allāh? Show me what they have created of the earth; or did they have partnership in [creation of] the heavens? Bring me a scripture [revealed] before this or a [remaining] trace of knowledge, if you should be truthful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرَءَيْتُم", "translit": "mُtْyَءَrَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَدْعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعْdَt", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَرُونِى", "translit": "àِnwُrَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَاذَا", "translit": "āَhdāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "خَلَقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "شِرْكٌ", "translit": "ٌkْrِhs", "root": "شرك"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱئْتُونِى", "translit": "àِnwُtْyʾٱ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "بِكِتَٰبٍ", "translit": "ٍbَٰtِkِb", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "قَبْلِ", "translit": "ِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "هَٰذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "أَثَٰرَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَrَٰhtَaʾ", "root": "اثر"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "عِلْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْlِʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "صَٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَٰṣ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "وَمَنْ أَضَلُّ مِمَّن يَدْعُوا۟ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ مَن لَّا يَسْتَجِيبُ لَهُۥٓ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ وَهُمْ عَن دُعَآئِهِمْ غَٰفِلُونَ ", "translation": "And who is more astray than he who invokes besides Allāh those who will not respond to him until the Day of Resurrection [i.e., never], and they, of their invocation, are unaware.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَنْ", "translit": "ْnَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَضَلُّ", "translit": "ُّlَḍَaʾ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِمَّن", "translit": "nَّmِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَدْعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعْdَy", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَسْتَجِيبُ", "translit": "ُbyِjgَtْsَy", "root": "جوب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَوْمِ", "translit": "ِmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَmَٰyِqْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "دُعَآئِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِyʾٓāَʿعُd", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "غَٰفِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِfَٰغ", "root": "غفل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "وَإِذَا حُشِرَ ٱلنَّاسُ كَانُوا۟ لَهُمْ أَعْدَآءً وَكَانُوا۟ بِعِبَادَتِهِمْ كَٰفِرِينَ ", "translation": "And when the people are gathered [that Day], they [who were invoked] will be enemies to them, and they will be deniers of their worship.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "حُشِرَ", "translit": "َrِhsُḥ", "root": "حشر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسُ", "translit": "ُsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَعْدَآءً", "translit": "ًءٓāَdْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَكَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَkَw", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِعِبَادَتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtَdāَbِʿعِb", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كَٰفِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِfَٰk", "root": "كفر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "وَإِذَا تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِمْ ءَايَٰتُنَا بَيِّنَٰتٍ قَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لِلْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ هَٰذَا سِحْرٌ مُّبِينٌ ", "translation": "And when Our verses are recited to them as clear evidences, those who disbelieve say of the truth when it has come to them, \"This is obvious magic.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تُتْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْtُt", "root": "تلو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَايَٰتُنَا", "translit": "āَnُtَٰyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بَيِّنَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰnِّyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لِلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlِl", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "جَآءَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "سِحْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْḥِs", "root": "سحر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مُّبِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "أَمْ يَقُولُونَ ٱفْتَرَىٰهُۖ قُلْ إِنِ ٱفْتَرَيْتُهُۥ فَلَا تَمْلِكُونَ لِى مِنَ ٱللَّهِ شَيْـًٔاۖ هُوَ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا تُفِيضُونَ فِيهِۖ كَفَىٰ بِهِۦ شَهِيدًۢا بَيْنِى وَبَيْنَكُمْۖ وَهُوَ ٱلْغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ", "translation": "Or do they say, \"He has invented it\"? Say, \"If I have invented it, you will not possess for me [the power of protection] from Allāh at all. He is most knowing of that in which you are involved.[1] Sufficient is He as Witness between me and you, and He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَقُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُqَy", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱفْتَرَىٰهُ", "translit": "ُhٰàَrَtْfٱ", "root": "فري"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِنِ", "translit": "ِnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱفْتَرَيْتُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُtْyَrَtْfٱ", "root": "فري"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "تَمْلِكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkِlْmَt", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لِى", "translit": "àِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "شَيْـًٔا", "translit": "āًٔـْyَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَaʾ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "تُفِيضُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḍyِfُt", "root": "فيض"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "فِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "كَفَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَfَk", "root": "كفي"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "شَهِيدًۢا", "translit": "āًۢdyِhَhs", "root": "شهد"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "بَيْنِى", "translit": "àِnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "وَبَيْنَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَnْyَbَw", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱلْغَفُورُ", "translit": "ُrwُfَغْlٱ", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "قُلْ مَا كُنتُ بِدْعًا مِّنَ ٱلرُّسُلِ وَمَآ أَدْرِى مَا يُفْعَلُ بِى وَلَا بِكُمْۖ إِنْ أَتَّبِعُ إِلَّا مَا يُوحَىٰٓ إِلَىَّ وَمَآ أَنَا۠ إِلَّا نَذِيرٌ مُّبِينٌ ", "translation": "Say, \"I am not something new among the messengers,[1] nor do I know what will be done with me or with you. I only follow that which is revealed to me, and I am not but a clear warner.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كُنتُ", "translit": "ُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِدْعًا", "translit": "āًʿعْdِb", "root": "بدع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلرُّسُلِ", "translit": "ِlُsُّrlٱ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَدْرِى", "translit": "àِrْdَaʾ", "root": "دري"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يُفْعَلُ", "translit": "ُlَʿعْfُy", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِى", "translit": "àِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أَتَّبِعُ", "translit": "ُʿعِbَّtَaʾ", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "يُوحَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَḥwُy", "root": "وحي"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "إِلَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "نَذِيرٌ", "translit": "ٌryِhdَn", "root": "نذر"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "مُّبِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "قُلْ أَرَءَيْتُمْ إِن كَانَ مِنْ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ وَكَفَرْتُم بِهِۦ وَشَهِدَ شَاهِدٌ مِّنۢ بَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ عَلَىٰ مِثْلِهِۦ فَـَٔامَنَ وَٱسْتَكْبَرْتُمْۖ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهْدِى ٱلْقَوْمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ", "translation": "Say, \"Have you considered: if it [i.e., the Qur’ān] was from Allāh, and you disbelieved in it while a witness from the Children of Israel has testified to something similar[1] and believed while you were arrogant...?\"[2] Indeed, Allāh does not guide the wrongdoing people.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرَءَيْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْyَءَrَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عِندِ", "translit": "ِdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَكَفَرْتُم", "translit": "mُtْrَfَkَw", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَشَهِدَ", "translit": "َdِhَhsَw", "root": "شهد"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "شَاهِدٌ", "translit": "ٌdِhāَhs", "root": "شهد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِّنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بَنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnَb", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِءَٰٓrْsِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مِثْلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlْhtِm", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "فَـَٔامَنَ", "translit": "َnَmāَٔـَf", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "وَٱسْتَكْبَرْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْrَbْkَtْsٱَw", "root": "كبر"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "يَهْدِى", "translit": "àِdْhَy", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِlَّٰẓlٱ", "root": "ظلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ لَوْ كَانَ خَيْرًا مَّا سَبَقُونَآ إِلَيْهِۚ وَإِذْ لَمْ يَهْتَدُوا۟ بِهِۦ فَسَيَقُولُونَ هَٰذَآ إِفْكٌ قَدِيمٌ ", "translation": "And those who disbelieve say of those who believe, \"If it had [truly] been good, they would not have preceded us to it.\" And when they are not guided by it, they will say, \"This is an ancient falsehood.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَوْ", "translit": "ْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "خَيْرًا", "translit": "āًrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "سَبَقُونَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnwُqَbَs", "root": "سبق"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَإِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَمْ", "translit": "ْmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَهْتَدُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُdَtْhَy", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فَسَيَقُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُqَyَsَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "هَٰذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِفْكٌ", "translit": "ٌkْfِiʾ", "root": "افك"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "قَدِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِdَq", "root": "قدم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "وَمِن قَبْلِهِۦ كِتَٰبُ مُوسَىٰٓ إِمَامًا وَرَحْمَةًۚ وَهَٰذَا كِتَٰبٌ مُّصَدِّقٌ لِّسَانًا عَرَبِيًّا لِّيُنذِرَ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوا۟ وَبُشْرَىٰ لِلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "And before it was the scripture of Moses to lead and as a mercy. And this is a confirming Book in an Arabic tongue to warn those who have wronged and as good tidings to the doers of good.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمِن", "translit": "nِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَبْلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كِتَٰبُ", "translit": "ُbَٰtِk", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِمَامًا", "translit": "āًmāَmِiʾ", "root": "امم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَرَحْمَةً", "translit": "ًẗَmْḥَrَw", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَهَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كِتَٰبٌ", "translit": "ٌbَٰtِk", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مُّصَدِّقٌ", "translit": "ٌqِّdَṣُّm", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لِّسَانًا", "translit": "āًnāَsِّl", "root": "لسن"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عَرَبِيًّا", "translit": "āًّyِbَrَʿع", "root": "عرب"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لِّيُنذِرَ", "translit": "َrِhdnُyِّl", "root": "نذر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ظَلَمُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُmَlَẓ", "root": "ظلم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَبُشْرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrْhsُbَw", "root": "بشر"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لِلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlِl", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ قَالُوا۟ رَبُّنَا ٱللَّهُ ثُمَّ ٱسْتَقَٰمُوا۟ فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ ", "translation": "Indeed, those who have said, \"Our Lord is Allāh,\" and then remained on a right course - there will be no fear concerning them, nor will they grieve.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رَبُّنَا", "translit": "āَnُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱسْتَقَٰمُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُmَٰqَtْsٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "خَوْفٌ", "translit": "ٌfْwَhk", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَحْزَنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnَzْḥَy", "root": "حزن"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ أَصْحَٰبُ ٱلْجَنَّةِ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَا جَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوا۟ يَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "Those are the companions of Paradise, abiding eternally therein as reward for what they used to do.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَصْحَٰبُ", "translit": "ُbَٰḥْṣَaʾ", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْجَنَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّnَjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "خَٰلِدِينَ", "translit": "َnyِdِlَٰhk", "root": "خلد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "جَزَآءًۢ", "translit": "ًۢءٓāَzَjg", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْʿعَy", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "وَوَصَّيْنَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ بِوَٰلِدَيْهِ إِحْسَٰنًاۖ حَمَلَتْهُ أُمُّهُۥ كُرْهًا وَوَضَعَتْهُ كُرْهًاۖ وَحَمْلُهُۥ وَفِصَٰلُهُۥ ثَلَٰثُونَ شَهْرًاۚ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُۥ وَبَلَغَ أَرْبَعِينَ سَنَةً قَالَ رَبِّ أَوْزِعْنِىٓ أَنْ أَشْكُرَ نِعْمَتَكَ ٱلَّتِىٓ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَىَّ وَعَلَىٰ وَٰلِدَىَّ وَأَنْ أَعْمَلَ صَٰلِحًا تَرْضَىٰهُ وَأَصْلِحْ لِى فِى ذُرِّيَّتِىٓۖ إِنِّى تُبْتُ إِلَيْكَ وَإِنِّى مِنَ ٱلْمُسْلِمِينَ ", "translation": "And We have enjoined upon man, to his parents, good treatment. His mother carried him with hardship and gave birth to him with hardship, and his gestation and weaning [period] is thirty months. [He grows] until, when he reaches maturity and reaches [the age of] forty years, he says, \"My Lord, enable me[1] to be grateful for Your favor which You have bestowed upon me and upon my parents and to work righteousness of which You will approve and make righteous for me my offspring. Indeed, I have repented to You, and indeed, I am of the Muslims.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَوَصَّيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَّṣَwَw", "root": "وصي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِوَٰلِدَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَdِlَٰwِb", "root": "ولد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِحْسَٰنًا", "translit": "āًnَٰsْḥِiʾ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "حَمَلَتْهُ", "translit": "ُhْtَlَmَḥ", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أُمُّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُّmُaʾ", "root": "امم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كُرْهًا", "translit": "āًhْrُk", "root": "كره"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَوَضَعَتْهُ", "translit": "ُhْtَʿعَḍَwَw", "root": "وضع"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كُرْهًا", "translit": "āًhْrُk", "root": "كره"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَحَمْلُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُlْmَḥَw", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَفِصَٰلُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُlَٰṣِfَw", "root": "فصل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ثَلَٰثُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhtَٰlَht", "root": "ثلث"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "شَهْرًا", "translit": "āًrْhَhs", "root": "شهر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "بَلَغَ", "translit": "َغَlَb", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أَشُدَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّdُhsَaʾ", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "وَبَلَغَ", "translit": "َغَlَbَw", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَرْبَعِينَ", "translit": "َnyِʿعَbْrَaʾ", "root": "ربع"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "سَنَةً", "translit": "ًẗَnَs", "root": "سنو"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "أَوْزِعْنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnْʿعِzْwَaʾ", "root": "وزع"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "أَنْ", "translit": "ْnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "أَشْكُرَ", "translit": "َrُkْhsَaʾ", "root": "شكر"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "نِعْمَتَكَ", "translit": "َkَtَmْʿعِn", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِtَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "أَنْعَمْتَ", "translit": "َtْmَʿعْnَaʾ", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "عَلَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "وَعَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿعَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "وَٰلِدَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَdِlَٰw", "root": "ولد"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "وَأَنْ", "translit": "ْnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "أَعْمَلَ", "translit": "َlَmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "صَٰلِحًا", "translit": "āًḥِlَٰṣ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "تَرْضَىٰهُ", "translit": "ُhٰàَḍْrَt", "root": "رضو"}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "وَأَصْلِحْ", "translit": "ْḥِlْṣَaʾَw", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "لِى", "translit": "àِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "ذُرِّيَّتِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِtَّyِّrُhd", "root": "ذرر"}, {"id": 40, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 41, "arabic": "تُبْتُ", "translit": "ُtْbُt", "root": "توب"}, {"id": 42, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 43, "arabic": "وَإِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 44, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 45, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسْلِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِlْsُmْlٱ", "root": "سلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ نَتَقَبَّلُ عَنْهُمْ أَحْسَنَ مَا عَمِلُوا۟ وَنَتَجَاوَزُ عَن سَيِّـَٔاتِهِمْ فِىٓ أَصْحَٰبِ ٱلْجَنَّةِۖ وَعْدَ ٱلصِّدْقِ ٱلَّذِى كَانُوا۟ يُوعَدُونَ ", "translation": "Those are the ones from whom We will accept the best of what they did and overlook their misdeeds, [their being] among the companions of Paradise. [That is] the promise of truth which they had been promised.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَتَقَبَّلُ", "translit": "ُlَّbَqَtَn", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَحْسَنَ", "translit": "َnَsْḥَaʾ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿع", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَنَتَجَاوَزُ", "translit": "ُzَwāَjgَtَnَw", "root": "جوز"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "سَيِّـَٔاتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtāَٔـِّyَs", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَصْحَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰḥْṣَaʾ", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْجَنَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّnَjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَعْدَ", "translit": "َdْʿعَw", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلصِّدْقِ", "translit": "ِqْdِّṣlٱ", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "يُوعَدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdَʿعwُy", "root": "وعد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "وَٱلَّذِى قَالَ لِوَٰلِدَيْهِ أُفٍّ لَّكُمَآ أَتَعِدَانِنِىٓ أَنْ أُخْرَجَ وَقَدْ خَلَتِ ٱلْقُرُونُ مِن قَبْلِى وَهُمَا يَسْتَغِيثَانِ ٱللَّهَ وَيْلَكَ ءَامِنْ إِنَّ وَعْدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقٌّ فَيَقُولُ مَا هَٰذَآ إِلَّآ أَسَٰطِيرُ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ ", "translation": "But one who says to his parents, \"Uff[1] to you; do you promise me that I will be brought forth [from the earth] when generations before me have already passed on [into oblivion]?\" while they call to Allāh for help [and to their son], \"Woe to you! Believe! Indeed, the promise of Allāh is truth.\" But he says, \"This is not but legends of the former peoples\" -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِوَٰلِدَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَdِlَٰwِl", "root": "ولد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أُفٍّ", "translit": "ٍّfُaʾ", "root": "افف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَّكُمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmُkَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَتَعِدَانِنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnِnāَdِʿعَtَaʾ", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَنْ", "translit": "ْnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أُخْرَجَ", "translit": "َjgَrْhkُaʾ", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "خَلَتِ", "translit": "ِtَlَhk", "root": "خلو"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْقُرُونُ", "translit": "ُnwُrُqْlٱ", "root": "قرن"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "قَبْلِى", "translit": "àِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَهُمَا", "translit": "āَmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يَسْتَغِيثَانِ", "translit": "ِnāَhtyِغَtْsَy", "root": "غوث"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَيْلَكَ", "translit": "َkَlْyَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ءَامِنْ", "translit": "ْnِmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَعْدَ", "translit": "َdْʿعَw", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "حَقٌّ", "translit": "ٌّqَḥ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "فَيَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَyَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "هَٰذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "إِلَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "أَسَٰطِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِṭَٰsَaʾ", "root": "سطر"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَّwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ حَقَّ عَلَيْهِمُ ٱلْقَوْلُ فِىٓ أُمَمٍ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِن قَبْلِهِم مِّنَ ٱلْجِنِّ وَٱلْإِنسِۖ إِنَّهُمْ كَانُوا۟ خَٰسِرِينَ ", "translation": "Those are the ones upon whom the word [i.e., decree] has come into effect, [who will be] among nations which had passed on before them of jinn and men. Indeed, they [all] were losers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَقَّ", "translit": "َّqَḥ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمُ", "translit": "ُmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْلُ", "translit": "ُlْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أُمَمٍ", "translit": "ٍmَmُaʾ", "root": "امم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "خَلَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlَhk", "root": "خلو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "قَبْلِهِم", "translit": "mِhِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْجِنِّ", "translit": "ِّnِjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَٱلْإِنسِ", "translit": "ِsnِiʾْlٱَw", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "خَٰسِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِsَٰhk", "root": "خسر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "وَلِكُلٍّ دَرَجَٰتٌ مِّمَّا عَمِلُوا۟ۖ وَلِيُوَفِّيَهُمْ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "And for all there are degrees [of reward and punishment] for what they have done, and [it is] so that He may fully compensate them for their deeds, and they will not be wronged.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلِكُلٍّ", "translit": "ٍّlُkِlَw", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دَرَجَٰتٌ", "translit": "ٌtَٰjgَrَd", "root": "درج"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿع", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَلِيُوَفِّيَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَyِّfَwُyِlَw", "root": "وفي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يُظْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْẓُy", "root": "ظلم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "وَيَوْمَ يُعْرَضُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ عَلَى ٱلنَّارِ أَذْهَبْتُمْ طَيِّبَٰتِكُمْ فِى حَيَاتِكُمُ ٱلدُّنْيَا وَٱسْتَمْتَعْتُم بِهَا فَٱلْيَوْمَ تُجْزَوْنَ عَذَابَ ٱلْهُونِ بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَسْتَكْبِرُونَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ ٱلْحَقِّ وَبِمَا كُنتُمْ تَفْسُقُونَ ", "translation": "And the Day those who disbelieved are exposed to the Fire [it will be said], \"You exhausted your pleasures during your worldly life and enjoyed them, so this Day you will be awarded the punishment of [extreme] humiliation because you were arrogant upon the earth without right and because you were defiantly disobedient.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَyَw", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُعْرَضُ", "translit": "ُḍَrْʿعُy", "root": "عرض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلنَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّnlٱ", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَذْهَبْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْbَhْhdَaʾ", "root": "ذهب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "طَيِّبَٰتِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِtَٰbِّyَṭ", "root": "طيب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "حَيَاتِكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkِtāَyَḥ", "root": "حيي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلدُّنْيَا", "translit": "āَyْnُّdlٱ", "root": "دنو"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَٱسْتَمْتَعْتُم", "translit": "mُtْʿعَtْmَtْsٱَw", "root": "متع"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بِهَا", "translit": "āَhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "فَٱلْيَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَyْlٱَf", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "تُجْزَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَzْjgُt", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "عَذَابَ", "translit": "َbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْهُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُhْlٱ", "root": "هون"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "تَسْتَكْبِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِbْkَtْsَt", "root": "كبر"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "بِغَيْرِ", "translit": "ِrْyَغِb", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "وَبِمَا", "translit": "āَmِbَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "تَفْسُقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqُsْfَt", "root": "فسق"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "وَٱذْكُرْ أَخَا عَادٍ إِذْ أَنذَرَ قَوْمَهُۥ بِٱلْأَحْقَافِ وَقَدْ خَلَتِ ٱلنُّذُرُ مِنۢ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِۦٓ أَلَّا تَعْبُدُوٓا۟ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَ إِنِّىٓ أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ", "translation": "And mention, [O Muḥammad], the brother of ʿAad,[1] when he warned his people in [the region of] al-Aḥqāf - and warners had already passed on before him and after him - [saying], \"Do not worship except Allāh. Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a terrible day.\"[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱذْكُرْ", "translit": "ْrُkْhdٱَw", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَخَا", "translit": "āَhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَادٍ", "translit": "ٍdāَʿع", "root": "عود"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَنذَرَ", "translit": "َrَhdnَaʾ", "root": "نذر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قَوْمَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِٱلْأَحْقَافِ", "translit": "ِfāَqْḥَaʾْlٱِb", "root": "حقف"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "خَلَتِ", "translit": "ِtَlَhk", "root": "خلو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلنُّذُرُ", "translit": "ُrُhdُّnlٱ", "root": "نذر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بَيْنِ", "translit": "ِnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَدَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَdَy", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَمِنْ", "translit": "ْnِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "خَلْفِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِfْlَhk", "root": "خلف"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "أَلَّا", "translit": "āَّlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "تَعْبُدُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُdُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "إِنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَخَافُ", "translit": "ُfāَhkَaʾ", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "عَلَيْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "عَذَابَ", "translit": "َbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "يَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "عَظِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِẓَʿع", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "قَالُوٓا۟ أَجِئْتَنَا لِتَأْفِكَنَا عَنْ ءَالِهَتِنَا فَأْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَآ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"Have you come to delude us away from our gods? Then bring us what you promise us, if you should be of the truthful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَجِئْتَنَا", "translit": "āَnَtْyʾِjgَaʾ", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِتَأْفِكَنَا", "translit": "āَnَkِfْaʾَtِl", "root": "افك"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَنْ", "translit": "ْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ءَالِهَتِنَا", "translit": "āَnِtَhِlāَء", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَأْتِنَا", "translit": "āَnِtْaʾَf", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "تَعِدُنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnُdِʿعَt", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "كُنتَ", "translit": "َtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "قَالَ إِنَّمَا ٱلْعِلْمُ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ وَأُبَلِّغُكُم مَّآ أُرْسِلْتُ بِهِۦ وَلَٰكِنِّىٓ أَرَىٰكُمْ قَوْمًا تَجْهَلُونَ ", "translation": "He said, \"Knowledge [of its time] is only with Allāh, and I convey to you that with which I was sent; but I see you [to be] a people behaving ignorantly.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّمَا", "translit": "āَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْعِلْمُ", "translit": "ُmْlِʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عِندَ", "translit": "َdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَأُبَلِّغُكُم", "translit": "mُkُغِّlَbُaʾَw", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أُرْسِلْتُ", "translit": "ُtْlِsْrُaʾ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnِkَٰlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَرَىٰكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkٰàَrَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "قَوْمًا", "translit": "āًmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "تَجْهَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَhْjgَt", "root": "جهل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "فَلَمَّا رَأَوْهُ عَارِضًا مُّسْتَقْبِلَ أَوْدِيَتِهِمْ قَالُوا۟ هَٰذَا عَارِضٌ مُّمْطِرُنَاۚ بَلْ هُوَ مَا ٱسْتَعْجَلْتُم بِهِۦۖ رِيحٌ فِيهَا عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ ", "translation": "And when they saw it as a cloud approaching their valleys, they said, \"This is a cloud bringing us rain!\" Rather, it is that for which you were impatient:[1] a wind, within it a painful punishment,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَأَوْهُ", "translit": "ُhْwَaʾَr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَارِضًا", "translit": "āًḍِrāَʿع", "root": "عرض"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُّسْتَقْبِلَ", "translit": "َlِbْqَtْsُّm", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَوْدِيَتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtَyِdْwَaʾ", "root": "ودي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَارِضٌ", "translit": "ٌḍِrāَʿع", "root": "عرض"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مُّمْطِرُنَا", "translit": "āَnُrِṭْmُّm", "root": "مطر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱسْتَعْجَلْتُم", "translit": "mُtْlَjgْʿعَtْsٱ", "root": "عجل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "رِيحٌ", "translit": "ٌḥyِr", "root": "روح"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "عَذَابٌ", "translit": "ٌbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أَلِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِlَaʾ", "root": "الم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "تُدَمِّرُ كُلَّ شَىْءٍۭ بِأَمْرِ رَبِّهَا فَأَصْبَحُوا۟ لَا يُرَىٰٓ إِلَّا مَسَٰكِنُهُمْۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِى ٱلْقَوْمَ ٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ ", "translation": "Destroying everything by command of its Lord. And they became so that nothing was seen [of them] except their dwellings. Thus do We recompense the criminal people.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تُدَمِّرُ", "translit": "ُrِّmَdُt", "root": "دمر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كُلَّ", "translit": "َّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "شَىْءٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِأَمْرِ", "translit": "ِrْmَaʾِb", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبِّهَا", "translit": "āَhِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَأَصْبَحُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُḥَbْṣَaʾَf", "root": "صبح"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يُرَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَrُy", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مَسَٰكِنُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُnِkَٰsَm", "root": "سكن"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "نَجْزِى", "translit": "àِzْjgَn", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِrْjgُmْlٱ", "root": "جرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "وَلَقَدْ مَكَّنَّٰهُمْ فِيمَآ إِن مَّكَّنَّٰكُمْ فِيهِ وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ سَمْعًا وَأَبْصَٰرًا وَأَفْـِٔدَةً فَمَآ أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُمْ سَمْعُهُمْ وَلَآ أَبْصَٰرُهُمْ وَلَآ أَفْـِٔدَتُهُم مِّن شَىْءٍ إِذْ كَانُوا۟ يَجْحَدُونَ بِـَٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ وَحَاقَ بِهِم مَّا كَانُوا۟ بِهِۦ يَسْتَهْزِءُونَ ", "translation": "And We had certainly established them in such as We have not established you, and We made for them hearing and vision and hearts [i.e., intellect]. But their hearing and vision and hearts availed them not from anything [of the punishment] when they were [continually] rejecting the signs of Allāh; and they were enveloped by what they used to ridicule.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَكَّنَّٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّٰnَّkَm", "root": "مكن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِيمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَّكَّنَّٰكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّٰnَّkَّm", "root": "مكن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَجَعَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَʿعَjgَw", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "سَمْعًا", "translit": "āًʿعْmَs", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَأَبْصَٰرًا", "translit": "āًrَٰṣْbَaʾَw", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَأَفْـِٔدَةً", "translit": "ًẗَdِٔـْfَaʾَw", "root": "فاد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَغْنَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَnْغَaʾ", "root": "غني"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "سَمْعُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُʿعْmَs", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أَبْصَٰرُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُrَٰṣْbَaʾ", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "وَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَفْـِٔدَتُهُم", "translit": "mُhُtَdِٔـْfَaʾ", "root": "فاد"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "يَجْحَدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdَḥْjgَy", "root": "جحد"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "بِـَٔايَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰyāَٔـِb", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَحَاقَ", "translit": "َqāَḥَw", "root": "حيق"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "بِهِم", "translit": "mِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "يَسْتَهْزِءُونَ", "translit": "َnwُءِzْhَtْsَy", "root": "هزا"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 27, "text": "وَلَقَدْ أَهْلَكْنَا مَا حَوْلَكُم مِّنَ ٱلْقُرَىٰ وَصَرَّفْنَا ٱلْءَايَٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُونَ ", "translation": "And We have already destroyed what surrounds you of [those] cities, and We have diversified the signs [or verses] that perhaps they might return [from disbelief].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَهْلَكْنَا", "translit": "āَnْkَlْhَaʾ", "root": "هلك"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "حَوْلَكُم", "translit": "mُkَlْwَḥ", "root": "حول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْقُرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrُqْlٱ", "root": "قري"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَصَرَّفْنَا", "translit": "āَnْfَّrَṣَw", "root": "صرف"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْءَايَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰyāَءْlٱ", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَعَلَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّlَʿعَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَرْجِعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعِjgْrَy", "root": "رجع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 28, "text": "فَلَوْلَا نَصَرَهُمُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّخَذُوا۟ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ قُرْبَانًا ءَالِهَةًۢۖ بَلْ ضَلُّوا۟ عَنْهُمْۚ وَذَٰلِكَ إِفْكُهُمْ وَمَا كَانُوا۟ يَفْتَرُونَ ", "translation": "Then why did those they took besides Allāh as deities by which to approach [Him][1] not aid them? But they had strayed [i.e., departed] from them. And that was their falsehood and what they were inventing.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَوْلَا", "translit": "āَlْwَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَصَرَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَrَṣَn", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱتَّخَذُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُhdَhkَّtٱ", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قُرْبَانًا", "translit": "āًnāَbْrُq", "root": "قرب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ءَالِهَةًۢ", "translit": "ًۢẗَhِlāَء", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ضَلُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّlَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "عَنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِفْكُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُkْfِiʾ", "root": "افك"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "يَفْتَرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَtْfَy", "root": "فري"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 29, "text": "وَإِذْ صَرَفْنَآ إِلَيْكَ نَفَرًا مِّنَ ٱلْجِنِّ يَسْتَمِعُونَ ٱلْقُرْءَانَ فَلَمَّا حَضَرُوهُ قَالُوٓا۟ أَنصِتُوا۟ۖ فَلَمَّا قُضِىَ وَلَّوْا۟ إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِم مُّنذِرِينَ ", "translation": "And [mention, O Muḥammad], when We directed to you a few of the jinn, listening to the Qur’ān. And when they attended it, they said, \"Listen attentively.\" And when it was concluded, they went back to their people as warners.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "صَرَفْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْfَrَṣ", "root": "صرف"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "نَفَرًا", "translit": "āًrَfَn", "root": "نفر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْجِنِّ", "translit": "ِّnِjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَسْتَمِعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعِmَtْsَy", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْقُرْءَانَ", "translit": "َnāَءْrُqْlٱ", "root": "قرا"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "حَضَرُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُrَḍَḥ", "root": "حضر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَنصِتُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُtِṣnَaʾ", "root": "نصت"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "قُضِىَ", "translit": "َàِḍُq", "root": "قضي"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَلَّوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَّlَw", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "قَوْمِهِم", "translit": "mِhِmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مُّنذِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِhdnُّm", "root": "نذر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 30, "text": "قَالُوا۟ يَٰقَوْمَنَآ إِنَّا سَمِعْنَا كِتَٰبًا أُنزِلَ مِنۢ بَعْدِ مُوسَىٰ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ يَهْدِىٓ إِلَى ٱلْحَقِّ وَإِلَىٰ طَرِيقٍ مُّسْتَقِيمٍ ", "translation": "They said, \"O our people, indeed we have heard a [recited] Book revealed after Moses confirming what was before it which guides to the truth and to a straight path.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰقَوْمَنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَmْwَqَٰy", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سَمِعْنَا", "translit": "āَnْʿعِmَs", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كِتَٰبًا", "translit": "āًbَٰtِk", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أُنزِلَ", "translit": "َlِznُaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بَعْدِ", "translit": "ِdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مُصَدِّقًا", "translit": "āًqِّdَṣُm", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لِّمَا", "translit": "āَmِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَدَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَdَy", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَهْدِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِdْhَy", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَإِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "طَرِيقٍ", "translit": "ٍqyِrَṭ", "root": "طرق"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "مُّسْتَقِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِqَtْsُّm", "root": "قوم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 31, "text": "يَٰقَوْمَنَآ أَجِيبُوا۟ دَاعِىَ ٱللَّهِ وَءَامِنُوا۟ بِهِۦ يَغْفِرْ لَكُم مِّن ذُنُوبِكُمْ وَيُجِرْكُم مِّنْ عَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ ", "translation": "O our people, respond to the Caller [i.e., Messenger] of Allāh[1] and believe in him; He [i.e., Allāh] will forgive for you your sins and protect you from a painful punishment.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰقَوْمَنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَmْwَqَٰy", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَجِيبُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbyِjgَaʾ", "root": "جوب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "دَاعِىَ", "translit": "َàِʿعāَd", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَءَامِنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnِmāَءَw", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَغْفِرْ", "translit": "ْrِfْغَy", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَكُم", "translit": "mُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ذُنُوبِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِbwُnُhd", "root": "ذنب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَيُجِرْكُم", "translit": "mُkْrِjgُyَw", "root": "جور"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَذَابٍ", "translit": "ٍbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَلِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِlَaʾ", "root": "الم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 32, "text": "وَمَن لَّا يُجِبْ دَاعِىَ ٱللَّهِ فَلَيْسَ بِمُعْجِزٍ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَلَيْسَ لَهُۥ مِن دُونِهِۦٓ أَوْلِيَآءُۚ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ فِى ضَلَٰلٍ مُّبِينٍ ", "translation": "But he who does not respond to the Caller of Allāh will not cause failure [to Him] upon earth, and he will not have besides Him any protectors. Those are in manifest error.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُجِبْ", "translit": "ْbِjgُy", "root": "جوب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "دَاعِىَ", "translit": "َàِʿعāَd", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَلَيْسَ", "translit": "َsْyَlَf", "root": "ليس"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِمُعْجِزٍ", "translit": "ٍzِjgْʿعُmِb", "root": "عجز"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَلَيْسَ", "translit": "َsْyَlَw", "root": "ليس"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "دُونِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَوْلِيَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَyِlْwَaʾ", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ضَلَٰلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَٰlَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مُّبِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 33, "text": "أَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا۟ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضَ وَلَمْ يَعْىَ بِخَلْقِهِنَّ بِقَٰدِرٍ عَلَىٰٓ أَن يُحْۦِىَ ٱلْمَوْتَىٰۚ بَلَىٰٓ إِنَّهُۥ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيرٌ ", "translation": "Do they not see that Allāh, who created the heavens and earth and did not fail in their creation, is able to give life to the dead? Yes. Indeed, He is over all things competent.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَوَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَرَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَrَy", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "خَلَقَ", "translit": "َqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضَ", "translit": "َḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَعْىَ", "translit": "َàْʿعَy", "root": "عيي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِخَلْقِهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhِqْlَhkِb", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بِقَٰدِرٍ", "translit": "ٍrِdَٰqِb", "root": "قدر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يُحْۦِىَ", "translit": "َàِۦْḥُy", "root": "حيي"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْمَوْتَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَtْwَmْlٱ", "root": "موت"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "بَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "قَدِيرٌ", "translit": "ٌryِdَq", "root": "قدر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 34, "text": "وَيَوْمَ يُعْرَضُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ عَلَى ٱلنَّارِ أَلَيْسَ هَٰذَا بِٱلْحَقِّۖ قَالُوا۟ بَلَىٰ وَرَبِّنَاۚ قَالَ فَذُوقُوا۟ ٱلْعَذَابَ بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَكْفُرُونَ ", "translation": "And the Day those who disbelieved are exposed to the Fire [it will be said], \"Is this not the truth?\" They will say, \"Yes, by our Lord.\" He will say, \"Then taste the punishment for what you used to deny.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَyَw", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُعْرَضُ", "translit": "ُḍَrْʿعُy", "root": "عرض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلنَّارِ", "translit": "ِrāَّnlٱ", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَلَيْسَ", "translit": "َsْyَlَaʾ", "root": "ليس"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بِٱلْحَقِّ", "translit": "ِّqَḥْlٱِb", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَرَبِّنَا", "translit": "āَnِّbَrَw", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "فَذُوقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqwُhdَf", "root": "ذوق"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابَ", "translit": "َbāَhdَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "تَكْفُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُfْkَt", "root": "كفر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 35, "text": "فَٱصْبِرْ كَمَا صَبَرَ أُو۟لُوا۟ ٱلْعَزْمِ مِنَ ٱلرُّسُلِ وَلَا تَسْتَعْجِل لَّهُمْۚ كَأَنَّهُمْ يَوْمَ يَرَوْنَ مَا يُوعَدُونَ لَمْ يَلْبَثُوٓا۟ إِلَّا سَاعَةً مِّن نَّهَارٍۭۚ بَلَٰغٌۚ فَهَلْ يُهْلَكُ إِلَّا ٱلْقَوْمُ ٱلْفَٰسِقُونَ ", "translation": "So be patient, [O Muḥammad], as were those of determination among the messengers and do not be impatient for them.[1] It will be - on the Day they see that which they are promised - as though they had not remained [in the world] except an hour of a day. [This is] notification. And will [any] be destroyed except the defiantly disobedient people?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱصْبِرْ", "translit": "ْrِbْṣٱَf", "root": "صبر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَمَا", "translit": "āَmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "صَبَرَ", "translit": "َrَbَṣ", "root": "صبر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أُو۟لُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزْمِ", "translit": "ِmْzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلرُّسُلِ", "translit": "ِlُsُّrlٱ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "تَسْتَعْجِل", "translit": "lِjgْʿعَtْsَt", "root": "عجل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كَأَنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnَaʾَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَرَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَrَy", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يُوعَدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdَʿعwُy", "root": "وعد"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَمْ", "translit": "ْmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "يَلْبَثُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُhtَbْlَy", "root": "لبث"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "سَاعَةً", "translit": "ًẗَʿعāَs", "root": "سوع"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "نَّهَارٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭrāَhَّn", "root": "نهر"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "بَلَٰغٌ", "translit": "ٌغَٰlَb", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "فَهَلْ", "translit": "ْlَhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "يُهْلَكُ", "translit": "ُkَlْhُy", "root": "هلك"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْمُ", "translit": "ُmْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱلْفَٰسِقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqِsَٰfْlٱ", "root": "فسق"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"11": [{"arabic": "جهله فإن الناس أعداء ما جهلوا قال تعالى وإذا لم يهتدوا به فسيقولون هذا إفك قديم قال الشاعر ومن يك ذا فم مر مريض ...", "english": "I say: Knowledge is like a torrent that is hostile to the elevated place — it flows only to the low ground. Thus knowledge is not attained except through humility and the casting of one's hearing [in attentive submission]. God — exalted is He — said: {«Indeed in that is a reminder for whoever has a heart or casts his hearing while present as a witness»} (Q 50:37). And the meaning of his being \"one having a heart\" is that he should be receptive to knowledge, comprehending it. But then the capacity for understanding does not avail him until he casts his hearing while being a present witness — present of heart — so that he may receive everything that is cast to him with excellence of listening, supplication, gratitude, joy, and acceptance of the benefaction.", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "section_title_ar": "Section 42", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Book I, Section 42: On the Duties of the Student (Ādāb al-Mutaʿallim)", "section_index": 42, "anchors": "- Root: ع ل م (ʿ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of knowing, perceiving a thing in its reality; the mark, trace, or sign by which one is guided.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العلم: إدراك الشيء بحقيقته\" — knowledge is the apprehension of a thing in its true reality, divided into apprehension of the essence and judgment upon it.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"هو من أعلام العلم الخافقه\" — he is among the lofty banners of knowledge. Metaphorical (majāz): \"خفيت معالم الطريق\" — the waymarks of the road are hidden, i.e., the traces by which one is guided.\n- Root: س م ع (s-m-ʿ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Hearing, listening; the ear; obedience and acceptance.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Hearing with attentive presence of heart, not merely the physical sensation of sound.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: auditory perception. Metaphorical: \"ألقى السمع\" — to cast one's hearing, i.e., to listen with full attentiveness and submission.\n- Root: ق ل ب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The heart; to turn, overturn, or transform a thing from one state to another.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — the turning of a thing from one face to another; the heart as that which is ever-turning between states.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" — to turn a thing from its face. Metaphorical: \"رجل قلب حول: يقلب الأمور ويحتال\" — a man who turns matters over and devises means.\n- Root: ب ح ر (b-ḥ-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The sea; vast expanse of water.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"أصل البحر: كل مكان واسع جامع للماء الكثير\" — the sea is every vast place gathering much water; then metaphorically applied to one who expands deeply into a domain.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Metaphorical: \"تبحر في العلم واستبحر فيه\" — he plunged deep into knowledge and expanded therein like a sea.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Bāb al-ḥaṣr wa-l-taqyīd bi-innamā (Restriction and Focused Predication) — the particle innamā restricts the predicate to the subject alone, negating all else; applied here to the exclusive path of the student's submission to the teacher's direction.", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Du'a"}], "13": [{"arabic": "في بالكلية غير الله ومعنى قوله تعالى الذين قالوا ربنا الله ثم استقاموا ولما كان الصراط المستقيم الذي لا يكمل التوحيد إلا بالاستقامة عليه أدق من الشعر وأخذ من السيف مثل الصراط الموصوف في الآخرة فلا ينفك بشر عن ميل عن الاستقامة ولو في أمر يسير إذ لا يخلو عن اتباع الهوى ولو في فعل قليل وذلك قادح في كمال التوحيد بقدر ميله عن الصراط المستقيم فذلك يقتضي لا محالة نقصانا في درجات القرب ومع كل نقصان ناران نار الفراق لذلك الكمال الفائت بالنقصان ونار جهنم كما وصفها القرآن فيكون كل مائل عن الصراط المستقيم معذبا مرتين من وجهين", "english": "The fire of Hell is the coldest of fires [in comparison to the fire of separation]. And you should not deny this in the world of the Hereafter, for it has a witnessed parallel in the world of this world. Indeed, one has been seen who was overcome by ecstasy (wajd) and walked upon fire and upon the roots of cane, his feet being cut, yet he did not feel it, due to the extreme dominance of what was in his heart. And you see the angry man, when anger overcomes him in battle, receiving wounds and not feeling them at that moment, because anger is a fire in the heart. The Messenger of God, peace and blessings be upon him, said: {«الغضب قطعة من النار»} \"Anger is a piece of fire.\" The burning of the heart (iḥtirāq al-fu'ād) is more severe than the burning of bodies, and the more severe annuls the sensation of the weaker, as you observe. For destruction from fire and the sword is only inasmuch as they separate between two parts that are linked one to the other by the bond of composition (ta'līf) possible in bodies. So that which separates between the heart and its Beloved, to which it is linked by a bond of composition far more firm than the composition of bodies, is more intensely painful—if you are among the people of insight (abṣār) and the people of hearts. And it is not far-fetched that he who has no heart should not perceive the severity of this pain and should deem it trivial in comparison to bodily pain. For a boy, if he were given the choice between the pain of being deprived of a ball and a polo-stick, and the pain of being deprived of the rank of a Sultan, he would not feel the pain of deprivation from the Sultan's rank at all, nor would he count that as a pain. And the enemy in the field with the polo-stick is more beloved to him than a thousand thrones of the Sultan with sitting upon them. Nay, even one overcome by the lust of the belly, if given the choice between porridge (harīsah) and sweets (ḥalwā) and between a beautiful deed by which he conquers enemies and delights friends, he would prefer the porridge and sweets. All of this is due to the absence of the meaning (maʿnā) by whose existence rank becomes beloved, and the presence of the meaning by whose existence food becomes delicious. This is for one whom the attributes of beasts and predators have enslaved, and in whom the attributes of the angels have not appeared—those attributes which are not suited by, nor delight in, anything but proximity to the Lord of the Worlds, and which are pained only by distance and the veil (ḥijāb). And just as taste is only in the tongue and hearing only in the ears, so this attribute is only in the heart. So he who has no heart has no such sense, like he who has no hearing or sight has no pleasure in melodies or the beauty of forms and colors. And not every human has a heart; were it so, the saying of God, Most High, would not be sound: {«إن في ذلك لذكرى لمن كان له قلب»} \"Indeed in that is a reminder for whoever has a heart\" (Q. 50:37). Thus He made the one who does not heed the Quran devoid of a heart. And by \"heart\" I do not mean this [organ] which the ribs of the chest encompass. Rather, I mean the secret (sirr) which is of the world of the Command (ʿālam al-amr). The flesh which is of the world of Creation (ʿālam al-khalq) is its Throne (ʿarsh), the chest is its Footstool (kursī), and the rest of the limbs are its domain and kingdom. And to God belongs the Creation and the Command altogether. But that secret, concerning which God, Most High, said: {«قل الروح من أمر ربي»} \"Say: The Spirit is of the Command of my Lord\" (Q. 17:85), is the commander and the king, because between the world of the Command and the world of Creation there is an ordering, and the world of the Command is commander over the world of Creation. It is the subtle divine reality (al-laṭīfah) which, when it is sound, the rest of the body is sound for its sake. Whoever knows it has known his own self, and whoever knows his own self has known his Lord. At that point, the servant smells the beginnings of the fragrance of the meaning folded under his saying, peace and blessings be upon him: {«إن الله خلق آدم على صورته»} \"God created Adam upon His image.\" He looks with the eye of mercy upon those who adhere to its literal wording and upon those who are obstinate in the path of its interpretation (ta'wīl). And even though His mercy for those adhering to the letter is greater than His mercy for the obstinate interpreters, because mercy is proportional to the affliction, and the affliction of those [literalists] is greater—even if they share in the affliction of being deprived of the reality of the matter—for the Reality (al-ḥaqīqah) is the bounty of God which He gives to whom He wills, and God is the Possessor of Great Bounty. And His Wisdom is singled out for whom He wills: {«ومن يؤت الحكمة فقد أوتي خيرا كثيرا»} \"And whoever is given wisdom has been given much good\" (Q. 2:269). Let us return to the purpose, for we have drawn out the length and lengthened the breath in a matter that is higher than the sciences of transactions (muʿāmalāt) which we intend in this book. It has become clear that the rank of destruction is only for the ignorant deniers. And the testimony of that from the Book of God and the Sunnah of His Messenger, peace and blessings be upon him, is beyond enumeration, so we have not cited it.", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "section_title_ar": "Section 930", "section_title_en": "The Ranks of the Hereafter: On the Distribution of Degrees and the States of the Saved, the Punished, and the Victorious", "section_index": 930, "anchors": "- Root: ح ر ق (ḥ-r-q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of burning, scorching, and the fire's consumption of its fuel.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The fire of the Hereafter (Nār) is a created reality, but its perception is tied to the spiritual state of the perceiver.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) for physical burning; metaphorical (Majaz) for the burning of the heart (iḥtirāq al-fu'ād) by overwhelming love or anger.\n- Root: ق ل ب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To turn, overturn, or transform a thing from one state to another.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The heart (Qalb) is the seat of perception and understanding, distinct from the physical organ.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for the physical heart; metaphorical for the spiritual subtlety (Laṭīfah) that is the locus of divine knowledge and love.\n- Root: ع ل م (ʿ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To know, to perceive a thing by its true nature.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Knowledge (ʿIlm) is the apprehension of a thing's reality, which is the basis for distinguishing the ranks of the believers.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for acquired knowledge; metaphorical for the \"unveiling\" (Kashf) knowledge granted to the knowers (ʿĀrifūn).\n- Sibawayh Rule: Restriction and Specification (Bāb al-Ḥaṣr wa al-Taqyīd bi-innamā) — Used to distinguish the specific referents of terms like \"heart\" (Qalb) and \"faith\" (Īmān), ensuring the precise meaning is not conflated with common usage.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وبقوله تعالى إن الذين قالوا ربنا الله ثم استقاموا بل هو معنى قولك لا إله إلا الله أى لا معبود ولا محبوب سواه فكل محبوب فإنه معبود فإن العبد هو المقيد والمعبود هو المقيد به وكل محب فهو مقيد بما يحبه ولذلك قال الله تعالى أرأيت من اتخذ إلهه هواه وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم أبغض إله عبد في الأرض الهوى ولذلك قال عليه السلام من قال لا إله إلا الله مخلصا دخل الجنة ومعنى الإخلاص أن يخلص قلبه لله فلا يبقى فيه شرك لغير الله فيكون الله محبوب قلبه ومعبود قلبه ومقصود قلبه فقط ومن هذا حاله فالدنيا سجنه لأنها مانع", "english": "The first: severing the attachments of this world and expelling love of other-than-God from the heart. For the heart is like a vessel: it cannot accommodate vinegar, for example, unless the water is first poured out of it. {God has not made for any man two hearts in his breast} [Al-Ahzab/4]. The perfection of love consists in loving God — mighty and majestic — with one's entire heart. As long as he turns toward other than Him, a corner of his heart is occupied with other than Him. To the extent that he is occupied with other than God, love of God diminishes from it; and to the extent that water remains in the vessel, the vinegar poured into it is diminished.", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "section_title_ar": "Section 1164", "section_title_en": "The Two Pillars of Love for God: Purification of the Heart and Strength of Knowledge", "section_index": 1164, "anchors": "- Root: ح ب ب (ḥ-b-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root denotes steadfastness and permanence; the heart's fixed attachment to its object.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Love (maḥabbah) is the soul's inclination toward what pleases it; its perfection is exclusive devotion, as in the verse {يحبهم ويحبونه} [Al-Ma'idah/54].\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) usage denotes the heart's clinging; metaphorical (majāz) usage extends to acts of obedience and yearning, culminating in 'ishq (intense passionate love) when it overwhelms the lover.\n- Root: خ ل ص (kh-l-ṣ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Purity from admixture; the essence of a thing freed from foreign elements.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Ikhlāṣ is the purification of intention so that no share of creation remains in it; it is the condition for the validity of the shahādah.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: clear, unmixed honey or water; metaphorical: the heart emptied of all rivals so that God alone occupies it.\n- Root: ز ه د (z-h-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Abstention from what is not essential; renunciation of the superfluous.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Asceticism (zuhd) is the heart's detachment from worldly goods, not merely the abandonment of possessions; it is a preparatory station (maqām) for love.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: disinterest in a thing; metaphorical: the soul's indifference to the ephemeral in favor of the eternal.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Restriction and Specification (Bāb al-Ḥaṣr wa al-Taqyīd bi-innamā) — The particle innamā restricts the predicate to the subject alone, as in \"إنما يكتسب العبد حب الله\" — affirming love's acquisition solely through specified means, negating all others.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Insight"}], "14": [{"arabic": "وقيل في قوله تعالى {فلا تعلم نفس ما أخفي لهم من قرة أعين جزاء بما كانوا يعملون} قيل كان عملهم الصيام لأنه قال {إنما يوفى الصابرون أجرهم بغير حساب} فيفرغ للصائم جزاؤه إفراغا ويجازف جزافا فلا يدخل تحت وهم وتقدير وجدير بأن يكون كذلك لأن الصوم إنما كان له ومشرفا بالنسبة إليه وإن كانت العبادات كلها له كما شرف البيت بالنسبة إلى نفسه والأرض كلها له لمعنيين أحدهما أن الصوم كف وترك وهو في نفسه سر ليس فيه عمل يشاهد وجميع أعمال الطاعات بمشهد من الخلق ومرأى والصوم لا يراه إلا الله عز وجل فإنه عمل في الباطن بالصبر المجرد والثاني أنه", "english": "To proceed: Fasting is one quarter of faith, by virtue of his saying, peace and blessings be upon him: \"Fasting is half of patience\" — and by virtue of his saying, peace and blessings be upon him: \"Patience is half of faith\" {«الإيمان»}. Then it is distinguished by a particular characteristic of its attribution to Allah the Exalted, above all the other pillars — for Allah the Exalted said, in what His Prophet narrated from Him, peace and blessings be upon him: \"Every good deed is multiplied tenfold up to seven hundred times, except fasting, for it is Mine, and I shall reward it.\" And Allah the Exalted has said: {«Only the patient shall be paid their reward in full without reckoning»} (Q 39:10). And fasting is half of patience — so its reward has surpassed the law of measure and reckoning. And sufficient for you in knowing its excellence is his saying, peace and blessings be upon him: \"By Him in whose hand is my soul, the change in the breath of the mouth of the fasting person is more fragrant to Allah than the scent of musk. Allah the Exalted says: 'He only abandons his appetite, his food, and his drink for My sake — so fasting is for Me, and I shall reward it.'\" And he said, peace and blessings be upon him: \"Paradise has a gate called al-Rayyān, through which none shall enter except the fasting ones.\" And the fasting person is promised the meeting with Allah the Exalted as a portion of his fasting. And he said, peace and blessings be upon him: \"For the fasting person there are two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast, and a joy when he meets his Lord.\" And he said, peace and blessings be upon him: \"Everything has a gate, and the gate of worship is fasting.\" And he said, peace and blessings be upon him: \"The sleep of the fasting person is worship.\" And Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that he, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"When the month of Ramaḍān enters, the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of the Fire are closed, the devils are chained, and a caller calls out: 'O seeker of good, come forth! O seeker of evil, desist!'\" And Wakīʿ said concerning His saying, the Exalted: {«Eat and drink in satisfaction for what you sent forth in the days past»} (Q 69:24) — these are the days of fasting, for in them they abandoned eating and drinking. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, gathered in the rank of divine boasting (mubāhāh) between renunciation of the world and fasting, saying: \"Allah the Exalted boasts to His angels of the young worshiper, saying: 'O young man who abandons his appetite for My sake, who devotes his youth to Me — you are to Me as some of My angels.'\" And he said, peace and blessings be upon him, concerning the fasting person: \"Allah the Exalted says: 'Look, O My angels, at My servant — he has abandoned his appetite, his pleasure, his food, and his drink for My sake.'\" And it was said concerning His saying, the Exalted: {«No soul knows what comfort has been concealed for them, as a reward for what they used to do»} (Q 32:17) — it was said: their deed was fasting, because He said: {«Only the patient shall be paid their reward in full without reckoning»} — so the reward of the fasting person is poured out upon him without measure, and is dealt out to him in bulk, not falling under any imagination or estimation.", "book_title": "Condemnation of Delusion", "section_title_ar": "Section 185", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Secrets of Fasting — Section 185: On the Excellence of Fasting and Its Distinction Among the Acts of Worship", "section_index": 185, "anchors": "- Root: صوم (ṣ-w-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core linguistic root meaning — abstention from any act, whether eating, speaking, or walking; a horse that refrains from movement or fodder is called ṣā'im.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological/Kalam semantic nuance — \"الصوم في الأصل: الإمساك عن الفعل\" — fasting is fundamentally the restraint of the self from action; it is an inward act of the heart, invisible to creation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical distinction — Haqiqah: the month of fasting, \"فمن شهد منكم الشهر فليصمه\" (Q 2:185); Majaz: \"صام الفرس على آريه\" — a horse standing still at its tether, refusing fodder, metaphorically \"fasting.\"\n- Root: عله (ʿ-l-h)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core linguistic root meaning — to feed or pasture; related to cultivation and nourishment.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological/Kalam semantic nuance — not directly attested in Mufradat for this root; the root pertains to the means by which the body is sustained, which is precisely what the fasting person abstains from.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical distinction — literal feeding and satiation; the fasting person's abstention from these becomes the very means of spiritual nourishment.\n- Root: الي (a-l-y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core linguistic root meaning — to convey a message; the angel (malak) is so named because the message is \"chewed\" (yu'lak) in the mouth, as a horse chews its bit.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological/Kalam semantic nuance — \"المألكة: الرسالة\" — the angelic function is the conveyance of divine communication; the fasting person's hunger narrows the channels through which the devil (who runs like blood through the veins) reaches the heart.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical distinction — literal conveyance of a message versus the metaphorical \"message\" of the devil's insinuation (waswās) through the pathways of the body.\n- Root: صبر (ṣ-b-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core linguistic root meaning — to restrain, to hold back in constriction; \"صبرت الدابة: حبستها بلا علف\" — to hold an animal back without fodder.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological/Kalam semantic nuance — \"الصبر: الإمساك في ضيق\" — patience is restraint within constriction; it is the holding of the soul upon what reason and law require, or from what they require it to abstain. Its names vary by context: in battle it is courage, in calamity it is patience proper.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical distinction — Haqiqah: \"صبرت على ما أكره وصبرت عما أحب\" — patience upon the disliked and patience from the beloved; Majaz: \"صبرت يمينه\" — to bind one's oath severely, and \"هو أصبر على الضرب من الأرض\" — more enduring of striking than the earth.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The particle innamā restricts and confines the predicate exclusively to its subject, as in the divine saying {«إنما يوفى الصابرون أجرهم بغير حساب»} and {«إنما يذر شهوته وطعامه وشرابه لأجلي»}, where the restriction elevates the restricted matter to a rank beyond all quantitative measure.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Condemnation of Delusion'", "badge": "Insight"}], "19": [{"arabic": "يقدر على الإخبار عنه لاشتغال همه به عن ثوبه وعن الحاضرين حواليه ولكل درجات مما عملوا فحظ كل واحد من صلاته بقدر خوفه وخشوعه وتعظيمه فإن موضع نظر الله سبحانه القلوب دون ظاهر الحركات ولذلك قال بعض الصحابة رضي الله عنهم يحشر الناس يوم القيامة على مثال هيئتهم في الصلاة من الطمأنينة والهدوء ومن وجود النعيم بها واللذة ولقد صدق فإنه يحشر كل على ما مات عليه ويموت على ما عاش عليه ويراعى في ذلك حال قلبه لا حال شخصه فمن صفات القلوب تصاغ الصور في الدار الآخرة ولا ينجو إلا من أتى الله بقلب سليم نسأل الله حسن التوفيق بلطفه وكرمه", "english": "The bond linking all these causes is faith (al-īmān) and certainty (al-yaqīn)—by which I mean these very knowledges we have mentioned. The meaning of their being \"certain\" is the absence of doubt and their full dominion over the heart, as has preceded in the exposition of certainty in the Book of Knowledge. And in proportion to one's certainty, the heart becomes humble (yakhsha'). For this reason, ʿĀ'ishah—may God be pleased with her—said: \"The Messenger of God—may God's peace and blessings be upon him—would converse with us and we with him; but when the time of prayer arrived, it was as though he knew us not, nor we him.\" It has also been related that God—Glory be to Him—revealed to Moses—peace be upon him: \"O Moses, when you remember Me, remember Me while your limbs tremble, and be, at the remembrance of Me, humble and tranquil. When you remember Me, place your tongue behind your heart. And when you stand before Me, stand as a lowly servant stands, and call upon Me with a fearful heart and a truthful tongue.\" It was also related that God—Exalted is He—revealed to him: \"Say to the disobedient ones of your community: Let them not remember Me, for I have sworn upon Myself that whoever remembers Me, I will remember him; so if they remember Me, I will remember them with a curse.\" This concerns a disobedient one who is not heedless in his remembrance—how then when heedlessness and disobedience are combined?", "book_title": "Mysteries of Prayer", "section_title_ar": "Section 135", "section_title_en": "Exposition of the Inner Meanings by Which the Life of Prayer is Perfected", "section_index": 135, "anchors": "- Root: خوف (kh-w-f)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core sense of fear, dread, apprehension of harm or punishment.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Fear (al-khawf) is the disturbance of the heart due to anticipation of something detestable; its theological counterpart is hope (al-rajā'), both being states consequent upon knowledge (ma'rifah).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqiqah) usage denotes fear of a tangible threat; metaphorical (majaz) usage extends to reverential awe (khashyah) of God's majesty, which is a state of the heart, not a bodily reaction.\n- Root: رجو (r-j-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To hope, expect, desire something good; the opposite of despair (ya's).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Hope (al-rajā') is the heart's tranquil expectation of a beloved matter after its causes have been secured; it is not mere wishful thinking (tamannī) but arises necessarily from certainty in God's promise and knowledge of His bounty.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage is anticipation of a favorable outcome; metaphorical usage in theology denotes the soul's reliance on God's grace (karam) as a motivating spiritual state.\n- Root: حيي (ḥ-y-y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Life; also shame, modesty (al-ḥayā'), derived from the sense of recoiling from base acts as if by a vital instinct.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Shame (al-ḥayā') is a state of the soul that restrains one from blameworthy acts, arising from the perception of one's own deficiency before the majesty of another; it is a moral faculty, not a mere emotion.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage is bashfulness before people; metaphorical usage is the reverential awe before God, born of the awareness of His omniscience over hidden thoughts.\n- Root: خشع (kh-sh-')\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To be lowly, submissive, humbled; physical stillness and lowering of the gaze.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Khushū' is the heart's humility and stillness before God, manifesting in the body's tranquility; it is the fruit of certainty (yaqīn).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage is bodily stillness; metaphorical usage is the heart's submissiveness, which is the true locus of prayer's life.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of 'Aṭf al-Bayān (Appositional Clarification) — The phrase \"أعني به\" (I mean by it) functions as explanatory apposition, specifying that the preceding term (al-īmān) is identical to the enumerated knowledges (al-ma'ārif), ensuring precise referential identity without ambiguity.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Mysteries of Prayer'", "badge": "Insight"}], "20": [{"arabic": "حال فبقدر ما يستوفي العبد من شهوته يخشى أن يقال له يوم القيامة {أذهبتم طيباتكم في حياتكم الدنيا واستمتعتم بها} وبقدر ما يجاهد نفسه ويترك شهوته يتمتع في الدار الآخر بشهواته قال بعض أهل البصرة نازعتني نفسي خبز أرز وسمكا فمنعتها فقويت مطالبتها واشتدت مجاهدتي لها عشرين سنة فلما مات قال بعضهم رأيته في المنام فقلت ماذا فعل الله بك قال لا أحسن أن أصف ما تلقاني به ربي من النعم والكرامات وكان أول شيء استقبلني به خبز أرز وسمكا وقال كل اليوم شهوتك هنيئا بغير حساب وقد قال تعالى {كلوا واشربوا هنيئا بما أسلفتم في الأيام الخالية} وكانوا قد أسلفوا ترك الشهوا", "english": "After that, [he mentioned] isfīdbāj (a meat stew), and Bishr said to him: \"Do you know of anything less than sikanjabīn (oxymel) that can take its place?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"I know.\" He said: \"What is it?\" He said: \"Chicory with vinegar.\" Then he said: \"Do you know of anything less than quince that can take its place?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"I know.\" He said: \"What is it?\" He said: \"Levantine carob.\" Then he said: \"Do you know of anything less than isfīdbāj that can take its place?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"I know — the water of chickpeas with cow's ghee serves in its place.\" Then ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said to him: \"You are more knowledgeable than I in medicine, so why did you ask me?\"", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "section_title_ar": "Section 647", "section_title_en": "On the Discipline of Appetite and the Etiquette of Eating — From the Revival of the Religious Sciences, Section 647", "section_index": 647, "anchors": "- Root: شهو (Shahiya)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is desire, craving, longing of the soul for something; appetite as an innate inclination.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological usage, شهوة (shahwah) denotes the lower appetitive drive of the soul (nafs) which must be disciplined and subordinated to reason and revelation; it is not inherently evil but becomes blameworthy when it dominates.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) — the natural craving for food, drink, or copulation. Metaphorical (Majaz) — the soul's excessive attachment to worldly pleasures that veils it from the divine.\n- Root: قلب (Qalb)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The heart; the organ of perception and understanding; that which fluctuates and turns (taqallub) between states.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The spiritual heart (al-qalb al-rūḥānī) is the locus of knowledge (maʿrifah), faith (īmān), and intention (niyyah); its hardness (qaswah) is the loss of receptivity to divine remembrance.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — the physical organ. Metaphorical — the seat of spiritual cognition and moral disposition; \"hardness of heart\" (qaswat al-qalb) is a metaphor for spiritual insensitivity.\n- Root: ضر (Ḍarūrah)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Necessity, compulsion, need; that which cannot be dispensed with.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In the scale of human need, ḍarūrah is the minimum required for the preservation of life and health; it is the limit to which the ascetic restricts his consumption.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — genuine need. Metaphorical — the legal principle that necessity permits what is otherwise restricted, but only to the extent of the need.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Condition and Exception (al-sharṭ wa al-jawāb) — The conditional structures in this passage (e.g., \"if he craves... then he should...\") establish normative sequences where the protasis (condition) governs the apodosis (result), indicating that the discipline of appetite is contingent upon the specific state of the soul.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Insight"}], "21": [{"arabic": "وإلى حالك ويغبطونك فى حسنك وجمالك والملائكة يمشون بين يديك ومن خلفك وينادون على رءوس الأشهاد هذا فلان بن فلان رضى الله عنه وأرضاه وقد سعد سعادة لا يشقى بعدها أبدا أفترى أن هذا المنصب ليس بأعظم من المكانة التى تنالها فى قلوب الخلق فى الدنيا بريائك ومداهنتك وتصنعك وتزينك فإن كنت تعلم أنه خير منه بل لانسبة له إليه فتوسل إلى إدراك هذه الرتبة بالإخلاص الصافى والنية الصادقة فى معاملتك مع الله فلن تدرك ذلك إلا به وإن تكن الأخرى والعياذ بالله بأن خرج من صحيفتك جريمة كنت تحسبها هينة وهى عند الله عظيمة فمقتك لأجلها فقا", "english": "Know that none is saved from the peril of the Scale except him who, in this world, called his own soul to account, and weighed therein — by the scale of the Sacred Law — his deeds, his words, his passing thoughts, and his glances, just as ʿUmar — may God be well pleased with him — said: \"Call yourselves to account before you are called to account, and weigh yourselves before you are weighed.\" Indeed, his calling himself to account consists in his repenting, before death, from every act of disobedience with a sincere repentance (tawbah naṣūḥ), and in his making up for what was neglected of his shortcomings regarding the obligatory commands of God — may He be exalted — and in his restoring rights to those he wronged, grain by grain, and in his seeking absolution from everyone whom he harmed by his tongue, his hand, or his evil suspicion harbored in his heart — and this by winning their hearts' contentment — until he dies with no outstanding wrong against him, nor any neglected obligation.", "book_title": "Remembrance of Death and Afterlife", "section_title_ar": "Section 1343", "section_title_en": "The Perils of the Scale and the Reckoning of Wrongs Against Others", "section_index": 1343, "anchors": "- Root: وزن (w-z-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is weighing, measuring, and balancing; al-mīzān (the Scale) is the instrument of equitable judgment.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological context, al-mīzān is the divine instrument of justice on the Day of Resurrection, weighing deeds to manifest equitable recompense, not a corporeal balance.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) usage denotes physical weighing; metaphorical (majāz) usage extends to moral and spiritual accounting, as in \"weighing one's deeds by the scale of the Sacred Law.\"\n- Sibawayh Rule: Conditional and Exceptive Constructions (الشّرط والاستثناء) — governing the protasis-apodosis structure in \"whoever's scales are heavy... whoever's scales are light,\" and the exceptive force in \"none is saved... except he who reckons.\"", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Remembrance of Death and Afterlife'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "الكعبة فقلت ومن هم قال الأكثرون أموالا إلا من قال هكذا وهكذا من بين يديه ومن خلفه وعن يمينه وعن شماله وقليل ما هم ما من صاحب إبل ولا بقر ولا غنم لا يؤدي زكاتها إلا جاءت يوم القيامة أعظم ما كانت وأسمنه تنطحه بقرونها وتطؤه بأظلافها كلما نفدت أخراها عادت عليه أولاها حتى يقضى بين الناس (1) وإذا كان هذا التشديد مخرجا في الصحيحين فقد صار من مهمات الدين الكشف عن أسرار الزكاة وشروطها الجلية والخفية ومعانيها الظاهرة والباطنة مع الاقتصار على ما لا يستغنى عن معرفته مؤدي الزكاة وقابضها وينكشف ذلك في أربعة فصول الفصل الأول في أنواع الزكاة وأسباب", "english": "To proceed: God Most High made alms (al-zakāh) one of the pillars of Islam, and joined its mention with prayer (al-ṣalāh), which is the loftiest of symbols. He said Most High: {«وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَآتُوا الزَّكَاةَ»} — \"And establish prayer and give alms.\" And he, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"Islam is built upon five: the testimony that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, the establishment of prayer, and the giving of alms.\" And He intensified the threat against those who fall short in it, saying: {«وَالَّذِينَ يَكْنِزُونَ الذَّهَبَ وَالْفِضَّةَ وَلَا يُنفِقُونَهَا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ فَبَشِّرْهُم بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ»} — \"And those who hoard gold and silver and do not spend them in the way of God — give them tidings of a painful chastisement.\" And the meaning of \"spending in the way of God\" is the payment of the due right of alms (zakāh).", "book_title": "Mysteries of Zakat", "section_title_ar": "Section 167", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Secrets of Alms (Zakat) — Section 167", "section_index": 167, "anchors": "- Root: زكا (Z-K-Y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Zakā al-zar'u yazkū zakā'an: it increased and grew.\" Core meaning: growth, increase, purification.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"The origin of zakāh is the growth that occurs through the blessing of God Most High... and from it is zakāh: what a person pays of God's right to the poor, so named for the hope of blessing in it, or for the purification (tazkiyah) of the soul, i.e., its growth.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqīqah): growth and increase. Metaphorical (majāz): the purification of wealth through payment of the obligatory due.\n- Root: نعم (N-'-M)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Na'ima 'ayshuhu: his life was pleasant.\" Core meaning: bounty, well-being, grace.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"Al-Ni'mah: the good state... and al-Ni'mah (with kasrah) is used for the genus, said of both little and much.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"Jallat ni'mat Allāh wa na'mā'uh\" — God's grace and bounty are immense. Metaphorical: \"Khāfat na'āmatuhum\" — their ostriches departed (i.e., they fled), showing the root's extended usage.\n- Root: ظهر (Z-H-R)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Zahara: to become apparent, to be victorious.\" Core meaning: back, outward appearance, manifestation.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"Al-Zahr: the back (body part)... and it is used metaphorically for the surface of the earth.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"Rajul muzhir: a man strong of back.\" Metaphorical: \"Qalabtu al-amra zahrān li-baṭn\" — I turned the matter over back and belly (examined it thoroughly).\n- Root: سرر (S-R-R)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Sarra: to conceal, to keep secret.\" Core meaning: secret, inner self, joy.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"Al-Isrār: the opposite of al-i'lān (declaring)... and al-sirr is the speech concealed in the soul.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"Asarra al-ḥadīth: he concealed the speech.\" Metaphorical: \"Aṭaytuka sirrah: I gave you its choicest part (the secret/core of something).\"\n- Sibawayh Rule: Bāb al-faṣl bayna al-jār wa al-majrūr (Prepositional Interposition) — The permissibility of interposing elements between a preposition and its object when the intervening clause is complete in itself, as in \"fa'āfa 'alayhim min ni'matihi mā...\" where the prepositional phrase is completed after an intervening relative clause.", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Mysteries of Zakat'", "badge": "Du'a"}, {"arabic": "عثراتي واحفظني من بين يدي ومن خلفي وعن يميني وعن شمالي ومن فوقي وأعوذ بك أن أغتال من تحتي (1) اللهم لا تؤمني مكرك ولا تولني غيرك ولا تنزع عني سترك ولا تنسني ذكرك ولا تجعلني من الغافلين (2) وقل اللهم أنت ربي لا إله إلا أنت خلقتني وأنا عبدك وأنا على عهدك ووعدك ما استطعت أعوذ بك من شر ما صنعت أبوء لك بنعمتك علي وأبوء بذنبي فاغفر لي فإنه لا يغفر الذنوب إلا أنت (3) ثلاث مرات وقل اللهم عافني في بدني وعافني في سمعي وعافني في بصري لا إله إلا أنت (4) ثلاث مرات وقل اللهم إني أسألك ال", "english": "\"Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, the Most Exalted, the Bestower (al-Wahhāb). There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the sovereignty and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful.\"", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "section_title_ar": "Section 251", "section_title_en": "The Fourth Chapter on Supplications Narrated from the Prophet (Peace Be Upon Him) and His Companions (May God Be Pleased with Them)", "section_index": 251, "anchors": "- Root: لهم (l-h-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of swallowing/ingesting (iltihām), from which ilhām (divine inspiration) derives—that which is cast into the heart\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الإلهام: إلقاء الشيء في الروع\" — divine inspiration is the casting of something into the inner faculty of consciousness (rawʿ), specifically from God and the higher assembly (malā aʿlā)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqīqah): \"ألهمه الله الخير: ألقاه في روعه\" (God inspired him with good: He cast it into his inner consciousness). Metaphorical (majāz): \"جيش لهام: يغتمر من يدخله\" (an overwhelming army that engulfs whoever enters it)\n- Root: غيب (gh-y-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: That which is hidden from sensory perception\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الغيب: مصدر غابت الشمس وغيرها: إذا استترت عن العين\" — that which is concealed from the eye; applied to all that is absent from the senses and from human knowledge. Notably: \"ويقال للشيء: غيب وغائب باعتباره بالناس لا بالله تعالى، فإنه لا يغيب عنه شيء\" (it is called ghayb relative to people, not relative to God, for nothing is hidden from Him)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"وتكلم بذلك عن ظهر الغيب\" (he spoke of that from behind the unseen). Metaphorical: \"أتونا في غابة أي في رماح كثيرة\" (they came to us in a thicket—i.e., amidst numerous spears like dense trees)\n- Root: علم (ʿ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Knowledge as the apprehension of a thing's reality\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العلم: إدراك الشيء بحقيقته\" — knowledge is the apprehension of a thing in its true reality; two types: apprehension of the essence of a thing, and judgment upon a thing regarding what exists for it or is negated from it\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"ما علمت بخبرك: ما شعرت به\" (I did not know of your news: I was not aware of it). \"وهو من أعلام العلم الخافقه\" (he is among the lofty banners of knowledge)\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — governing the permissible separation between the preposition and its object for rhetorical emphasis, as in the construction \"عالم الغيب والشهادة\" where the attributive relationship is maintained through the genitive construction (iḍāfah)", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'On Invocations and Supplications'", "badge": "Du'a"}], "29": [{"arabic": "إلى قومهم منذرين {فقالوا إنا سمعنا قرآنا عجبا يهدي إلى الرشد فآمنا به ولن نشرك بربنا أحدا} فكل من آمن به فقد وفق ومن قال به فقد صدق ومن تمسك به فقد هدي ومن عمل به فقد فاز وقال تعالى {إنا نحن نزلنا الذكر وإنا له لحافظون} ومن أسباب حفظه في القلوب والمصاحف استدامة تلاوته والمواظبة على دراسته مع القيام بآدابه وشروطه والمحافظة على ما فيه من الأعمال الباطنة والآداب الظاهرة وذلك لا بد من بيانه وتفصيله وتنكشف مقاصده في أربعة أبواب الباب الأول في فضل القرآن وأهله الباب الثاني ف", "english": "Praise be to God, who has bestowed His favor upon His servants through His sent Messenger (peace be upon him) and His revealed Book — falsehood cannot approach it from before it or from behind it; it is a revelation (tanzīl) from the Wise, the Praiseworthy {«تَنْزِيلٌ مِنْ حَكِيمٍ حَمِيدٍ»}. Through it, the path of reflection (iʿtibār) has been widened for the people of understanding, by virtue of what it contains of narratives and reports; and through it, the way of the upright course and the straight path (al-ṣirāṭ al-mustaqīm) has been made clear, by virtue of what it details of rulings and distinguishes between the lawful (ḥalāl) and the unlawful (ḥarām). It is the illumination and the light; through it is deliverance from delusion; in it is healing for what is in the breasts. Whoever opposes it among the tyrants, God crushes him; and whoever seeks knowledge in other than it, God leads him astray. It is the firm rope of God (ḥabl Allāh al-matīn), His manifest light, the trustworthy handhold (al-ʿurwah al-wuthqā), and the most faithful refuge. It encompasses the little and the much, the small and the great. Its wonders do not come to an end, nor do its marvels reach a limit. No delimitation (taḥdīd) encompasses its benefits according to the people of knowledge, nor does the frequency of repetition wear it out according to the people of recitation. It is that which guided the first and the last. When the jinn heard it, they did not delay in turning to their people as warners, saying: {«فَقَالُوا إِنَّا سَمِعْنَا قُرْآنًا عَجَبًا * يَهْدِي إِلَى الرُّشْدِ فَآمَنَّا بِهِ وَلَنْ نُشْرِكَ بِرَبِّنَا أَحَدًا»} (\"Indeed, we have heard a wondrous Quran; it guides to right conduct, so we have believed in it, and we will never associate anyone with our Lord.\") So whoever believes in it has been granted success (tawfīq); whoever speaks by it has spoken truthfully; whoever clings to it has been guided; and whoever acts by it has attained felicity (fawz). And God, the Exalted, says: {«إِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا الذِّكْرَ وَإِنَّا لَهُ لَحَافِظُونَ»} (\"Indeed, We — it is We who have sent down the Remembrance, and indeed, We are its Preservers.\") Among the means of its preservation (ḥifẓ) in hearts and in codices (maṣāḥif) is the constancy of its recitation (tilāwah) and perseverance in its study, along with the fulfillment of its etiquettes (ādāb) and conditions, and the safeguarding of what it contains of inward works (aʿmāl bāṭinah) and outward etiquettes (ādāb ẓāhirah). This cannot be done without its exposition and detailing; its aims unfold in four chapters (abwāb):", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "section_title_ar": "Section 220", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Etiquettes of Quran Recitation — Section 220: The Excellence of the Quran and Its People", "section_index": 220, "anchors": "- Root: نزل (n-z-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"نزل: انحطاط من علو إلى سفل\" — descent from a height to a lower place; the setting down of a thing in a place.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النزول في الأصل هو انحطاط من علو... وإنزال الله تعالى نعمه ونقمه على الخلق، وإعطاؤهم إياها\" — the descent of the Quran is a divine act of sending down (tanzīl) from the highest station, carrying with it the very mercy and address of God.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Haqiqah (literal): \"نزل من علو إلى سفل\" — physical descent. Majaz (metaphorical): \"وأنزل الله الغيث، وأنزل الكتاب\" — the \"sending down\" of revelation is a metaphorical extension denoting divine bestowal and elevation of the recipient, not spatial movement.\n- Root: حفظ (ḥ-f-ẓ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الحفظ: الحِراسة والاستظهار\" — guarding, preserving, and keeping watch over a thing.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الحفظ: ضبط الشيء عن أن يذهب أو يضيع\" — the securing of a thing against loss or corruption; divine preservation (ḥifẓ) is an act of sovereign care.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Haqiqah: guarding a physical object. Majaz: \"حفظ الله فلانًا\" — divine protection from spiritual harm and error.\n- Root: تلو (t-l-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"التلاوة: الاتباع، ثم سميت القراءة تلاوة لأنها تتبع الآيات حرفًا حرفًا\" — following in sequence; recitation is so named because the reader follows the verses letter by letter.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"التلاوة: الإتيان بالشيء متتابعًا\" — the bringing of a thing in succession; recitation of the Quran is the sequential utterance of its verses in devotion.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Haqiqah: following behind. Majaz: \"تلا الكتاب\" — reciting, as the tongue follows the written text.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The rule governing the separation of a preposition from its object by an intervening clause, as in «لا يأتيه الباطل من بين يديه ولا من خلفه», where the prepositional phrases are distributed across the sentence for rhetorical emphasis and comprehensiveness.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Insight"}], "35": [{"arabic": "محبوبها ثم لم يرض إلا أن يكلفني ما كلفهم فقال فاصبر كما صبر أولو العزم من الرسل والله مالي بد من طاعته وإني والله لأصبرن كما صبروا بجهدي ولا قوة إلا بالله (6) وروي عن عمر رضي الله عنه أنه حين فتح عليه الفتوحات قالت له ابنته حفصة رضي الله عنها البس ألين الثياب إذا وفدت عليك الوفود من الآفاق ومر بصنعة طعام تطعمه وتطعم من حضر فقال عمر يا حفصة ألست تعلمين أن أعلم الناس بحال الرجل أهل بيته فقالت بلى قال ناشدتك الله هل تعلمين أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم لبث في النبوة كذا وكذا سنة لم يشبع هو ولا أهل بيته غد", "english": "Allah the Exalted said: {فخرج على قومه في زينته} [He went out to his people in his adornment] up to His saying, the Exalted: {وقال الذين أوتوا العلم ويلكم ثواب الله خير لمن آمن} [And those who had been given knowledge said, \"Woe to you! The reward of Allah is better for he who believes.\"] Thus He attributed renunciation (al-zuhd) to the learned, and described its people as possessing knowledge—and this is the ultimate praise. And He said, the Exalted: {أولئك يؤتون أجرهم مرتين بما صبروا} [Those will be given their reward twice for what they patiently endured], and it came in the exegesis (al-tafsīr) that this refers to renunciation of the world. And He said, Mighty and Majestic: {إنا جعلنا ما على الأرض زينة لها لنبلوهم أيهم أحسن عملا} [Indeed We have made that which is on the earth adornment for it that We may test them as to which of them is best in deed]. It was said its meaning is: which of them is most renunciant (azhad) in it. So He described renunciation as being among the most excellent of deeds. And He said, the Exalted: {من كان يريد حرث الآخرة نزد له في حرثه ومن كان يريد حرث الدنيا نؤته منها وما له في الآخرة من نصيب} [Whoever desires the harvest of the Hereafter—We increase for him in his harvest. And whoever desires the harvest of this world—We give him from it, but he has no share in the Hereafter]. And He said, the Exalted: {ولا تمدن عينيك إلى ما متعنا به أزواجا منهم زهرة الحياة الدنيا لنفتنهم فيه ورزق ربك خير وأبقى} [And do not extend your eyes to that which We have given enjoyment to categories of them—the splendor of the life of this world—that We may test them thereby. And the provision of your Lord is better and more enduring]. And He said, the Exalted: {الذين يستحبون الحياة الدنيا على الآخرة} [Those who prefer the life of this world over the Hereafter]—thus He described the disbelievers with that. So its understood implication (mafhūmuhu) is that the believer is the one characterized by its opposite, namely, that he prefers the Hereafter over the life of this world. [PageV04P219]", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "section_title_ar": "Section 1090", "section_title_en": "The Book of Renunciation (Kitāb al-Zuhd) — Section on the Virtue of Despising the World", "section_index": 1090, "anchors": "- Root: زهد (z-h-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of abstaining, forsaking, and turning away from something, deeming it insignificant and paltry.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance: الزهد is the voluntary turning of the heart away from the world (al-dunyā) as a deliberate act of spiritual preference for the Hereafter, not mere physical poverty.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage denotes abstention from a thing due to its worthlessness; Metaphorical (Majaz) usage in the religious context signifies the heart's detachment from worldly allurements while the body may still function within it.\n- Root: دنا (d-n-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Nearness, proximity; the world (al-dunyā) is so named for its closeness and lower station relative to the Hereafter.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): الدنو: القرب بالذات أو بالحكم; al-dunyā is the lower, nearer abode, contrasted with the ultimate and enduring one.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: spatial or temporal nearness; Metaphorical: the world as the inferior, immediate realm that precedes the eternal one.\n- Root: عقل (ʿ-q-l) — implied in \"مفهومه\" (its understood implication)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Understanding, intellect, that which binds and restrains.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The intellect perceives the conceptual implication (mafhūm) of a statement, deriving the necessary opposite or corollary.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the articulated text; Metaphorical: the understood converse (mafhūm al-mukhālafah) which the author here employs to establish the believer's trait.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The periodic structure of the author's argumentation, where the governing verb (e.g., \"قال تعالى\") is separated from its quoted object by lengthy parenthetical citations, mirrors the classical allowance for interposition to maintain rhetorical flow and emphasis.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 250, 3626]], "2": [[1, 400, 1763], [2, 1763, 2978], [3, 2978, 3474], [4, 3474, 4453], [5, 4453, 5940], [6, 5940, 7403]], "3": [[1, 400, 1100], [2, 1100, 2769], [3, 2769, 4984], [4, 4984, 6680], [5, 6680, 7784], [6, 7784, 10358], [7, 10358, 11583], [8, 11583, 13064], [9, 13064, 14330], [10, 14330, 16349], [11, 16349, 18274], [12, 18274, 19917], [13, 19917, 22020], [14, 22020, 24013], [15, 24013, 25898]], "4": [[1, 400, 1045], [2, 1045, 2949], [3, 2949, 4136], [4, 4136, 5879], [5, 5879, 6465], [6, 6465, 7490], [7, 7490, 8647], [8, 8647, 10463], [9, 10463, 12016], [10, 12016, 13891], [11, 13891, 14477], [12, 14477, 15883], [13, 15883, 16528], [14, 16528, 17378], [15, 17378, 18316], [16, 18316, 19048], [17, 19048, 21458], [18, 21458, 23392], [19, 23392, 24740], [20, 24740, 25751], [21, 25751, 26762], [22, 26762, 28725], [23, 28725, 29516], [24, 29516, 30911], [25, 30911, 31922], [26, 31922, 32860], [27, 32860, 33505], [28, 33505, 34677], [29, 34677, 36660]], "5": [[1, 400, 1337], [2, 1337, 2475], [3, 2475, 3666], [4, 3666, 5553], [5, 5553, 6088], [6, 6088, 7025], 